   "text": "The Inference Tax: What Trading Systems Reveal About Energy-Aware AI\n\nThe fastest accelerator in a two-minute benchmark can become a completely different system forty-five minutes into a live session.\nAverage latency might hold steady, and mean power may even drop. But the true warning signals show up where it hurts: p99.99 latency, useful output rate, thermal margin, and clock-limit exposure.\nThat performance gap is the inference tax.\nMy latest technical white paper introduces two testable operating concepts:\n * Energy-Aware Computing: Measuring energy per useful output\u2014never power in isolation.\n * Power-Thermal-Aware Scheduling: Keeping latency-sensitive inference strictly inside a validat",
